      },
      "text": "Vd = plasma volume (~3L)          → stays in blood (heparin, proteins)\n  Vd = ECF (~12–14L)                → polar, doesn't enter cells\n  Vd = TBW (~42L)                   → crosses into cells\n  Vd >> 42L (100s–1000s L)          → extensive tissue binding (chloroquine, amiodarone)"
    },
    {
