      },
      "text": "Protein binding:\n  Albumin: binds acidic drugs (warfarin, phenytoin, NSAIDs)\n  α1-acid glycoprotein (AGP): binds basic drugs (lidocaine, propranolol)\n  Only free (unbound) drug is pharmacologically active\n  Displacement interactions (e.g., warfarin displaced by NSAIDs) → transient ↑ free drug"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#019",
      "path": [
