      "text": "### Metabolism"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#021",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:medicine:00-overview, git-history:medicine:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "medicine/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "00 - Medicine and Pharmacology Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nPhase I reactions: oxidation/reduction/hydrolysis\n  CYP450 enzymes (liver microsomes — ER membrane):\n    CYP3A4: ~50% of drugs; inducible by rifampin, carbamazepine, St. John's wort\n    CYP2D6: codeine → morphine; polymorphic (UM/EM/IM/PM)\n    CYP2C9: warfarin, phenytoin, NSAIDs\n    CYP2C19: omeprazole, clopidogrel (prodrug activation); PM = ~15% Asians\n    CYP1A2: theophylline, caffeine; induced by smoking"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#022",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:medicine:00-overview, git-history:medicine:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "medicine/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "00 - Medicine and Pharmacology Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Phase II reactions: conjugation (glucuronidation/sulfation/acetylation/glutathione)\n  Make drug more water-soluble → renal/biliary excretion\n  UDP-glucuronosyltransferases (UGTs) most important\n  N-acetyltransferase (NAT2): INH, hydralazine, procainamide; polymorphic (fast/slow acetylators)"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#023",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:medicine:00-overview, git-history:medicine:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "medicine/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "00 - Medicine and Pharmacology Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Prodrugs require metabolism for activation:\n  Clopidogrel → active thiol (CYP2C19); PMs don't respond\n  Codeine → morphine (CYP2D6); UMs → toxic morphine levels\n  Enalapril → enalaprilat (esterases)\n  Valacyclovir → acyclovir (gut/liver esterases)\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#024",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
